<item><title>Morocco secures Norway carbon-credit deal for renewable energy</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ma/morocco-secures-norway-carbon-credit-deal-for-renewable-d40d2b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ma/morocco-secures-norway-carbon-credit-deal-for-renewable-d40d2b/</guid><category>Morocco</category><description>Norway will buy credits for up to 8.78 million tons of verified emission reductions from Moroccan projects between 2027 and 2036.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:32:17 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ma.jpg" length="33258" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ma.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Morocco tightens African tomato exports as prices fall in Europe</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ma/morocco-tightens-african-tomato-exports-as-prices-fall-in-47f5d6/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ma/morocco-tightens-african-tomato-exports-as-prices-fall-in-47f5d6/</guid><category>Morocco</category><description>At Rungis, Moroccan tomatoes now fetch €1.10 to €1.30 per kilogram, down from €1.80 to €2 as shipments rise and sales slow.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:03:09 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ma.jpg" length="33258" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ma.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
